  "Episode 2 cues: what happens on screen in each beat, step by step, keyed by the beat IDs of ep2/outline.json and ep2/script.fountain.",
  "Step forms as in ep1/cues.json.  A visual may carry 'delay' (seconds after its step starts) and 'phase' (which part of a multi-step visual plays now).",
  "The diagrams are drawn from math_objects.json and from build_math_objects.py's definitions, never from sets typed here.  Sets and counts written in a cue ('points', 'completes', 'result', 'hexad', 'count', 'total', ...) are claims: check_outline.py recomputes each one and stops on a mismatch.",
  "The board holds one diagram at a time (Fano plane, Euler's clock, the kitten triangle, the three views); morph_layout changes it, cell by cell where the labels carry over.  Euler's twelve points are drawn as a clock: hours 0 to 10 round the dial, infinity at the center where the hand is pinned."
 ],
